  "title": "Berlin Conference",
  "summary": "Fifteen states, including the major European powers, the United States and the Ottoman Empire, met in Berlin on German chancellor Otto von Bismarck's initiative, with no African societies represented. The General Act of 26 February 1885 guaranteed free trade and navigation on the Congo and Niger, set 'effective occupation' as the standard for claims, and recognised Leopold II's Congo Free State.",
